Spoilers ahead...

Once you know what a genocide scroll is, you should _never_ (IMHO) read it
without either blessing it or cursing it first.  This can be done with
potions of holy water and unholy water that you make at alters.  If you
bless the scroll by #dipping it into holy water, you can then genocide an
entire class of similar monsters, such as liches.  These are pretty nasty
to deal with, and include liches, master liches, and demiliches.  This is
a great way to remove all the monsters you don't want to deal with at once,
but you can wipe out all the high point monsters (such as trolls) if you
aren't careful and relegate yourself to never being able to add much to your
score.  You could genocide all dragons with a blessed scroll, but then how
would you obtain dragon scale mail without a wand of wishing?  Generally, I
genocide only Liches as a class of monster.  If you read the scroll prior
to knowing what it it and it asks you what you want to get rid of, you should
make sure you know if it was uncursed or cursed (blessed will ask you what 
class of monster you want, so you will know it was blessed).  If it was
uncursed, you can only genocide one type of monster.  If it was cursed, you
will create several of that type of monster around you.  Be careful.

Scrolls of genocide are quite powerful.  I usually use them in a cursed mode,
since I can get them to create lots of one type of monster.  The type I
_always_ create are wraiths, since these allow me to increase an entire
experience level at once by eating a corpse.  I always make sure I'm at max
hit points and am wielding a good weapon before I read the cursed genocide
scroll, but then I go for it and make as many wraiths as I can.  Get rid of
your pet during this part, they eat those valuable corpses.  If you have to,
strand your pet on another level or shut the door to keep it out of a room.
Wraiths don't always leave corpses and you want to eat every single one that
you can.


